In article <1994Apr28.182112.588@beaver.cs.washington.edu> thomask@lynx.cs.washington.edu (Thomas K. Schonhoff) writes:
> How about a new intrinsic/curse called the Midas Touch?
> It would work like confuse monster (duration more like blessed confuse...)
> where everything you pick up turns to a pile of gold roughly equal to its
> current shop value?
>
> I picture it happening after you sit on a throne, in particular, although
> a nasty little scroll would be just as unpleasant and far more frequent.
> "You have the golden touch!" or "You may already be really wealthy" --
> something like that.  It would expire after far too many turns.

I like it!!

Points to think about:
- Objects already held by the player should probably not turn into
  gold.  That would be too cruel, to lose all one's possessions in
  one turn.
- I suppose you could eat food off the ground without turning it into
  gold.  The curse is probably bad enough without totally preventing
  one from getting any more food.
- How about this... if a player hits a monster with bare hands, and
  the monster is not stone-resistant, the monster is turned to gold.
  This could just be a pile of gold, but it would be cooler if it
  was a "golden statue of a lizard", which could be broken up with
  a pick-axe into gold pieces.
- Why not make the amount of gold that objects turn into
  proportional to the weight of the object, rather than its value?
  Then boulders would be great things to pick up if you could
  (unlikely), whereas picking up a dilithium crystal would be a
  tragedy.

